  "chapter": {
    "number": 93,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(94) A Psalm of David for the fourth day of the week."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is a God of vengeance; the God of vengeance",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 184
          },
          {
            "text": "has declared himself.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be you exalted, you that judge the earth: render a reward to the proud.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How long shall sinners, O Lord, how long shall sinners boast?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They will utter and speak unrighteousness; all the workers of iniquity will speak so.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have afflicted your people, O Lord, and hurt your heritage.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have slain the widow and fatherless, and murdered the stranger.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they said, The Lord shall not see, neither shall the God of Jacob understand.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Understand now, you⌃ simple among the people; and you⌃ fools, at length be wise.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He that planted the ear, does he not hear? or he that formed the eye, does not he perceive?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He that chastises the heathen, shall not he punish, even he that teaches man knowledge?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord knows the thoughts of men, that they are vain.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the man whoever you shall chasten, O Lord, and shall teach him out of your law;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to give him rest from evil days, until a pit be digged for the sinful one.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "until righteousness return to judgment, and all the upright in heart shall follow it. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who will rise up for me against the transgressors? or who will stand up with me against the workers of iniquity?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If the Lord had not helped me, my soul had almost sojourned in Hades.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If I said, My foot has been moved;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "your mercy, O Lord, helped me. O Lord, according to the multitude of my griefs within my heart, your consolation have",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 185
          },
          {
            "text": "soothed my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Shall the throne of iniquity have fellowship with you, which frames mischief by an ordinance?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They will hunt for the soul of the righteous, and condemn innocent blood.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the Lord was my refuge; and my God the helper of my hope.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he will recompense to them their iniquity and their wickedness: the Lord our God shall utterly destroy them.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 184,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. plural, bis.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 93,
          "verse": 1
        }
